{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786481692,"nonce":"eoH+DzhjSZKgIkk+5SCufSS6hCQ=","title":"**What is wrong.** README.md:120-123 says: *\"test/{contract,load}/  ⚠️ still a `doc.go` and no test. `test/load/` in particular claims the 5 000-alert storm batch that CONTEXT.md §6 says to write BEFORE the feature handling it. Treat these two as a plan, not as coverage.\"* README.md:137-138 then lists G1 as **enforced** via `go test ./test/contract/` and G2 as **enforced** via `go test ./test/contract/server/`. Both statements are on the same page, twelve lines apart.","message":"**The demonstration.** `test/contract/` holds nine `_test.go` files: `coverage_test.go` (the ratchet that binds every `operationId` to a named test), `dto_schema_test.go`, `envelope_test.go`, `openapi_doc_test.go`, `tenancy_test.go`, `schema/schema_test.go`, and `server/{conformance,plan,world}_test.go`. `test/load/` holds `storm_test.go`, `driver_test.go`, `env_test.go` and a 15.9 KB `RESULTS.md`. The 5 000-alert storm batch the Layout section calls a plan is written and has recorded results. The README understates its own coverage — the rarer direction of this error, and still a page that contradicts itself.\n\nSeparately, README.md:88-92 raises a question and leaves it open: *\"pkg/alertkey/  ⚠️ EMPTY — a doc.go and nothing else. The canonical label serialisation and the identity keys it describes actually live in `internal/alerts/domain`, the shared kernel, and CONTEXT.md §5.2b says this package does not exist. Delete it or amend CONTEXT.md; both cannot be true.\"* `pkg/alertkey/doc.go` is still the only file under `pkg/`, and CONTEXT.md:191 still reads *\"`pkg/alertkey` does not exist — `pkg/` is reserved for `otoclient`.\"*\n\n**Why it matters.** README.md:128-129 sets the standard itself: *\"Enforcement is worth stating precisely, because this repository has previously claimed gates it did not have.\"* The Layout section fails that standard in the inverse direction, and the cost is real navigation error — a contributor adding a contract test reads \"still a `doc.go` and no test\" and either duplicates the ratchet or concludes the gate table is stale. The `pkg/alertkey` entry is the smaller half but the more embarrassing one: the README asks a direct question whose answer has been available since the line was written.\n\n**Resolution.** CONTEXT.md:191 is correct and stands; `pkg/alertkey` is deleted, and the README's Layout entries for `pkg/alertkey/`, `test/contract/` and `test/load/` are corrected to describe the tree as it is. This ticket is the record of that decision — the change itself is in flight.\n\n**Where.** README.md:88-92 (`pkg/alertkey`), README.md:120-123 (the Layout claim), README.md:137-138 (the contradicting gate rows), `pkg/alertkey/doc.go` (the only file under `pkg/`), CONTEXT.md:191 (correct, unchanged).\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** `pkg/` contains no `alertkey`, and the README's Layout entries for `test/contract/` and `test/load/` name the tests that are there instead of calling them a plan.","files":null}]}